# One pattern per line. Use for one-off exclusions that don't fit
# lychee.toml's regex `exclude` list (e.g., a single flaky vendor URL).
#
# Add an explanation comment above each entry so the next reviewer
# knows why it's here.

# windsorcli.github.io is the website repo; not public yet, so the
# URL 404s from GitHub's public API. Remove this once the repo is
# published.
^https://github\.com/windsorcli/windsorcli\.github\.io

# ADR-0001's own stack lists contexts/{lifecycle,environment-injection,
# trusted-folders} as a trio; only the latter two were ever written. The
# skill docs quote lifecycle.md as a worked example of the guide-tier
# voice regardless — that's a real content gap for the docs owner to
# close, not a stale link to silently fix. Remove this once the page
# exists.
content/contexts/lifecycle\.md$
